  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A uniform rod of length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> is acted upon by a force&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;in a gravity-free region, as shown in the figure. If the area of cross-section of the rod is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and it's Young's modulus is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math>, then the elastic potential energy stored in the rod due to&nbsp;elongation is<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/1222222222222222222.JPG\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 70px;\" /></p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
